  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2801640,
    "dDurationMs": 10439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yes. If you watch that, it's not just frying an egg, putting it on rice, adding soy sauce and sesame oil and mixing it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2812079,
    "dDurationMs": 20480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You fry the egg on very high heat until it's crispy. From the beginning? Yes. And then turn off the heat in the pan, and when the pan has cooled down a bit, splash soy sauce into it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2832559,
    "dDurationMs": 15000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and almost burn half of the soy sauce. Yes. From that half-burned soy sauce, you get that kind of charred flavor, that nuance? It makes a difference with just one step. So I'm really eating it deliciously. I am."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2847559,
    "dDurationMs": 14601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, since when have you been eating this fixed? It's been over a month, I think? Still, it's recent. That's fine. Simple. Yes. Just eat it there with seaweed too."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2862160,
    "dDurationMs": 19480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I secretly add one more thing to what Chef Baek Jong-won does, and when I heat up the pan, I put oil in it and heat it up, right. To make the pan hot, but I don't use vegetable oil, I use avocado oil anyway."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2881640,
    "dDurationMs": 19000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Wow. Yes. But then. Because it's good for your body? Because it's good for your body. But then I add about a 2cm block of butter, let's say? Not too much and not too little. I melt the butter in that oil beforehand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2900640,
    "dDurationMs": 10159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Butter? Yes, yes. You use avocado oil because it's good for your body? Add 2cm of butter. It's not 2cm. About 1.5cm."
